The .meta file allows you to add authors, ratings, warnings, links, and credits.

If you add 'author:' before your name, it will display in the author section./NOBR
If you instead write 'authors:' it will display 'Authors: {meta_authors}' instead of 'Author: {meta_author}'.

Write 'rating: {rating}' to add a rating./NOBR
Ratings are: g, t, e, a./NOBR
G = General Audiences, T = Teen, E = Explicit, A = Adult

Write 'links: {your links}' to add links to your pages.

Write 'warnings: {your warnings}' to add warnings.

Write 'credits: {your credits}' to add credits.

A fully-filled-out .meta file would look like this:/CLRB

author: benheroblaw/NOBR/CONT
rating: t/NOBR/CONT
links: https://benheroblaw.github.io/NOBR/CONT/ESC
warnings: swearing/NOBR/CONT
credits: benheroblaw for coding the whole thing/CONT

And display as this:
Author:   benheroblaw/NOBR/CONT
Rating:   Teen/NOBR/CONT
Links:    https://benheroblaw.github.io/ESC/NOBR/CONT
Warnings: swearing/NOBR/CONT
Credits:  benheroblaw for coding the whole thing/NOBR/CONT